#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0252-C expect=violation domain=ADSL
#note "Positive control for the ADSL half of the AD0252 split - same Check as PMDA-AD0252-A, different Scope.Data_Structures. AVALCA1N seeds one expansion (y=1) and the disjunction is true, so the rule fires. Dataset granularity -> exactly 1 violation for the two rows, reported at row=1 by the BroadcastFold dataset-level path. AVALCA1N is present, so the expanded Output_Variable resolves by value from data row 1."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 AVALCA1N=1
dataset ADSL structure=ADSL
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col AGE      type=Num
col SAFFL    type=Char
col AVALCA1N type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 56 | Y | 1
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | 64 | Y | 2
